{"repository": "zed-industries/zed", "task_candidate_id": 27114, "repository_id": 319, "issue_number": 65743, "github_issue_id": 5894836775, "html_url": "https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/65743", "created_at": "2026-10-17T04:25:43+00:00", "author_association": null, "title": "GPUI: inappropriate RGBA alpha handling", "body_text": "<https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/322cd509dcccaee1f6bc44725d270598ae8171ad/crates/gpui/src/color.rs>

The file contains the following code:

```rs
impl Rgba {
    /// Create a new [`Rgba`] color by blending this and another color together
    pub fn blend(&self, other: Rgba) -> Self {
        if other.a >= 1.0 {
            other
        } else if other.a <= 0.0 {
            *self
        } else {
            Rgba {
                r: (self.r * (1.0 - other.a)) + (other.r * other.a),
                g: (self.g * (1.0 - other.a)) + (other.g * other.a),
                b: (self.b * (1.0 - other.a)) + (other.b * other.a),
                a: self.a,
            }
        }
    }
```

The alpha compositing logic here is clearly incorrect. This causes some noticeable bugs with semi-transparent themes.

## Example

As shown below, the Git gutter colors are completely invisible with these settings:

<img width="1321" height="1118" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb39b28d-daea-43af-b73d-014f2570e7e1" />

After switching to a fully opaque background, the Git gutter becomes visible:

<img width="1344" height="1119" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/08fa280d-480a-46e1-8353-743f5b19cad5" />

This is caused by the above incorrect alpha compositing logic.

## Fix

The fix actually requires very little code:

<https://github.com/Sha1rholder/zed/commit/58485b0d498b96d0dc4ac0ecca4c15250ca2aef3>

```rs
impl Rgba {
    /// Create a new [`Rgba`] color by blending this and another color together
    pub fn blend(&self, other: Rgba) -> Self {
        if other.a >= 1.0 {
            other
        } else if other.a <= 0.0 {
            *self
        } else {
            let background_alpha = self.a * (1.0 - other.a);
            let alpha = other.a + background_alpha;
            Rgba {
                r: (self.r * background_alpha + other.r * other.a) / alpha,
                g: (self.g * background_alpha + other.g * other.a) / alpha,
                b: (self.b * background_alpha + other.b * other.a) / alpha,
                a: alpha,
            }
        }
    }
```

However, this will certainly be a BREAKING CHANGE! It may break many transparent themes that rely on the previous behavior! Still, I personally believe this issue should be fixed sooner rather than later.

