I configured a layout where I used the strider plugin in the two panes of a tab. The cwd of the two striders is set to two different directories respectively: Folder A's cwd is configured as /Users/waylon/tmp/a, and Folder B's cwd is configured as /Users/waylon/tmp/b.

```
layout {
    tab_template name="striders-test" cwd="/Users/waylon/tmp"{
        pane size=1 borderless=true {
            plugin location="tab-bar"
        }
        pane split_direction="vertical" {
            pane size="30%" split_direction="horizontal" {
                pane name="Folder A" {
                    plugin location="strider" {
                        cwd "/Users/waylon/tmp/a"
                    }                            
                }
                pane name="Folder B" {
                    plugin location="strider" {
                        cwd "/Users/waylon/tmp/b"
                    }                
                }
            }
            children
        }
        pane size=1 borderless=true {
            plugin location="status-bar"
        } 
    }

    striders-test name="striders test" 
}
```

After creating a new session through this layout, I found that the cwds of the two striders are swapped: Folder A's path displays the content of /Users/waylon/tmp/b, and Folder B's path displays the content of /Users/waylon/tmp/a.

