One of my sessions ended up serialized with a `session-layout.kdl` containing no terminal panes. I was surprised to discover that this kept me from using a session as I expected. I'm not sure how layout got into that state in the first place, but I was able to reproduce the issue as follows:

1. Create a resurrectable session by writing the following contents to a `session-layout.kdl` in `~/.cache/zellij/contract_version_1/session_info/$session/session-layout`:

   ```kdl
   layout {
       tab name="topgrade" {
           pane size=1 borderless=true {
               plugin location="zellij:tab-bar"
           }
           pane borderless=true {
               plugin location="zellij:status-bar"
           }
       }
   }
   ```

   As a concrete example, you can create a session named `repro` by writing the above to `~/.cache/zellij/contract_version_1/session_info/repro/session-layout.kdl`.

2. Run `zellij attach ...` for the session, i.e., `zellij attach repro`, and observe that it prints `Bye from Zellij!` and exits immediately.

