body_text:
A background plugin loaded through load_plugins can miss PermissionRequestResult(Granted) during fresh-session startup when its permission is already cached.

In this reproduction, the same plugin loaded in a visible pane receives the callback. The terminal and stock tab bar also work.

Expected: both plugin instances receive the permission result, including when permission is already cached.

## Minimal reproduction

Create a small probe:

``` sh
cargo new --bin permission-probe --name probe
cd permission-probe
cargo add "zellij-tile@=0.44.3"
```

Replace src/main.rs with:

```rust
use std::collections::BTreeMap;
use zellij_tile::prelude::*;

#[derive(Default)]
struct State {
    role: String,
    granted: bool,
}
register_plugin!(State);

impl ZellijPlugin for State {
    fn load(&mut self, config: BTreeMap<String, String>) {
        self.role = config.get("role").cloned().unwrap_or_default();
        eprintln!("STARTUP_PROBE LOAD {} {:?}", self.role, get_plugin_ids());
        subscribe(&[EventType::PermissionRequestResult, EventType::ModeUpdate]);
        request_permission(&[PermissionType::ReadApplicationState]);
    }

    fn update(&mut self, event: Event) -> bool {
        if let Event::PermissionRequestResult(status) = event {
            self.granted = status == PermissionStatus::Granted;
            eprintln!("STARTUP_PROBE PERMISSION {} {:?}", self.role, status);
        }
        true
    }

    fn render(&mut self, _: usize, _: usize) {
        println!("PERMISSION_CALLBACK={}", self.granted);
    }
}
```

Build it:

```sh
rustup target add wasm32-wasip1
cargo build --release --target wasm32-wasip1
```

Save the following as repro.kdl in the project directory. Replace /absolute/path/permission-probe with the project’s absolute path:

```
layout_dir "/absolute/path/permission-probe"
default_layout "/absolute/path/permission-probe/repro.kdl"
default_shell "/bin/bash"
show_startup_tips false
show_release_notes false

load_plugins {
    "file:/absolute/path/permission-probe/target/wasm32-wasip1/release/probe.wasm" {
        role "background"
    }
}

layout {
    tab name="probe" {
        pane size=1 borderless=true {
            plugin location="zellij:tab-bar"
        }
        pane size=2 borderless=true {
            plugin location="file:/absolute/path/permission-probe/target/wasm32-wasip1/release/probe.wasm" {
                role "pane"
            }
        }
        pane command="/bin/bash" {
            args "-c" "printf TERMINAL_READY; sleep 9999"
        }
    }
}
```

From a terminal outside Zellij:

1. Start a session:

`zellij --config /absolute/path/permission-probe/repro.kdl --session permission-seed`
2. Approve the background plugin’s permission prompt with y, then quit with Ctrl-q.
3. Start a different fresh session with the same config:

`zellij --config /absolute/path/permission-probe/repro.kdl --session permission-repro`
4. Inspect the second session’s STARTUP_PROBE log entries.

Observed, with plugin IDs omitted here:

```
STARTUP_PROBE LOAD background …
STARTUP_PROBE LOAD pane …
STARTUP_PROBE PERMISSION pane Granted
```

The background callback does not arrive after waiting more than 20 seconds. The visible probe displays PERMISSION_CALLBACK=true, and the terminal displays TERMINAL_READY.

The expected additional entry is:

```
STARTUP_PROBE PERMISSION background Granted
```

Check after the second session’s LOAD entries: the log may also contain permission results from the first session.

## Other relevant information

- Linux x86_64; binary reports zellij 0.46.0.
- Tested upstream commit: 333d7898a840314e41d3cc9d2a264a1b9732bb7b, with its original lockfile.
- Native build: Rust 1.96.0, development profile, using --locked --no-default-features --features web_server_capability.
- Applying a local nine-line startup fix in wasm_bridge.rs makes both instances receive the callback with this reproduction.
- Possibly related: [#4982 (https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/issues/4982)](https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/issues/4982) and [#4990 (https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/pull/4990)](https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/pull/4990). This reproduction begins with cached permission.

Not tested on macOS, official/default-feature release binaries, or against PR #4990.

